Minimal Optimum is a working principle of Spiral Civilization: we begin with the smallest structure capable of enabling the next meaningful stage of development. We then learn from what happens, recognize what is missing, and use that knowledge to build the next version.
Higher Order is a form of organization emerging at a higher level of systemic complexity. An order that is natural and functional at one evolutionary stage may continue to operate at the next, while becoming increasingly inadequate to its new complexity. Higher Order describes the emergence of organizational forms capable of structuring that next level.
Higher Quality Order describes not a higher level of complexity, but a higher quality of organization within a given level of complexity.
Different orders can exist at the same civilizational level while producing radically different trajectories — from destructive, exploitative and corrupt structures toward increasingly intelligent, lawful, noble and multisymbiotic ones.
Higher Quality Order asks which forms of organization move from Zero toward the Best Possible.
The Best Possible is the highest-quality possibility that can be recognized from the present field of reality, knowledge and available choices.
The Perfect Spiral represents the Best Possible trajectory of development — the path through which each stage reaches the quality that enables the next evolutionary possibility to emerge.
Beginner’s Mind is the attitude of entering a new evolutionary threshold without assuming that the structures and rules of the previous stage remain adequate for the next one.
Point Zero is the primary point of reference of conscious navigation: “I am” — the beginning of the axes of experienced time, space and perceived reality.
The Best Possible Field is the field of possibilities in which what exists, what we recognize ourselves to be, and what we may become can be explored in relation to the Best Possible.
Potentiality Fields are fields of capacities, qualities and possibilities that an entity, relationship or system can bring into a larger whole.
Field of Potency describes the effective capacity of a person, project or system to make possibilities real through knowledge, abilities, relationships, resources, participation and alignment.
Multisymbiotic Systems are configurations in which relationships between multiple participants are designed to increase benefits, capacities and possibilities across the whole system.